evaluate.py: Because the original code only calls apply operation when it hits a + or -,
the last number is never actually evaluated in the function.

optimize.py: In lines 23 through 25, the variable attempt was getting updated three times.
The last update completely changed the variable instead of adding on to the end of it.

puntuation.py: The if statement checking if the character was a punctuation needed to be
false in order for the character to be added to the result string, not true. Previously,
it was just returning all of the punctuations in the string instead of the other way around.
